Scope: preserve red annular rear lenses when lamps are off, illuminate their existing geometry when on, and soften only declared wheel and lower-trim material roughness. The licensed GLB remains 8296356 bytes, SHA-256 fa889f70cd9c35d6831d7c81b9e647382dc1c59cd71a77bca2030c87a8dc308d. No cabin, new vehicle geometry, or additional 3D models are included.

Release changes only the unique gate marker, this existing release marker, and a focused public-material capture/upload step in the existing CI smoke workflow. Application/asset bytes are identical to the approved candidate. Acceptance requires this exact Railway release SUCCESS, matching public HTML and every JS/CSS byte, live focused material proof, and a real cloud-browser public UI check within its WebGL capabilities. Restore all 14 original watch patterns after live acceptance, then follow every triggered CI run to a terminal state. Software-renderer proof is not physical-device performance evidence.
